---
title: Shortcut
description: Show the keys of any action as <kbd>, always in sync with the active keymap.
---

<script lang="ts">
	import { ApiReference } from '#lib/index.ts';
</script>

`Shortcut.Root` renders the keyboard shortcut of a keymap action (`'markup.highlight'`, `'view.zoomIn'`, `'nav.back'`…). It reads the keymap from the nearest `Annotations.Root` or `Viewer.Root`, so overrides are reflected automatically.

```svelte
<button>Highlight <Shortcut.Root action="markup.highlight" /></button>
<!-- <kbd data-pdf-shortcut="markup.highlight"><kbd data-pdf-key>H</kbd></kbd> -->
```

Use the `child` / `children` snippets (`{ label, keys }`) to render your own key caps. `comboLabel(keymap, action)` gives the same label as text.

